# check-paths.sh exemption list -- one path prefix per line.
# Rule: every entry says **why it is exempt and when it goes away**. A temporary exemption with a
# task number counts; an open-ended one does not.

# -- usually exempt for good --
src/                       # example IPs and subnets in source are content, not machine configuration
archive/                   # frozen history; not one word of it should change
claude-outputs/            # scratch area: screenshots, reports, records -- the facts as they were then
product/                   # the Requester's own words are kept verbatim

# -- temporary exemptions go here, **each must carry a task number** --
# <path>/                  # <why> -> T-<number>. Delete this line when it is done

# The exemption list should be as SHORT as possible: every line is a hole where the criterion does not apply.
#   Anything a criterion can solve should not be exempted — e.g. a tool's own output directory should be handled by
#   making the guard **skip git-ignored paths**, not by a line here.
